How does the mandible contribute to the overall structure and function of the human skull?
The mandible, or lower jawbone, contributes to the overall structure and function of the human skull by forming the lower jaw and holding the lower teeth in place. It is the only movable bone of the skull, allowing for the movement of the jaw and enabling the human to speak, eat, and perform other functions that require the coordination of the mouth and teeth. The mandible also serves as a key component of the facial skeleton, which, along with the cranium, makes up the skull.
