What was the purpose and significance of the British Empire Exhibition held in London in 1925?
The purpose of the British Empire Exhibition held in London in 1924-1925 was to:

* Stimulate trade
* Strengthen the bonds within the Empire
* Demonstrate British greatness both abroad and at home

The significance of the exhibition was that it was the largest exhibition ever staged anywhere, costing £12 million, and it brought together 56 territories of the Empire with displays and pavilions, aiming to promote unity and understanding among the British colonies.
