The original animated series that "The Pebbles and Bamm-Bamm Show" is a spin-off of is "The Flintstones". It is the first spin-off series derived from "The Flintstones", minus the theatrical film "The Man Called Flintstone" in 1966. The show was produced by Hanna-Barbera Productions, with William Hanna and Joseph Barbera as executive producers, and Charles A. Nichols as the director. The series follows teenage Pebbles Flintstone and Bamm-Bamm Rubble as they encounter problems with growing up in the fictional town of Bedrock. The show originally aired for one season on CBS from September 11, 1971 to January 1, 1972.
