What is the structure of the British parliament?
The British parliament is bicameral and consists of three parts: 

1. The Sovereign (the Queen-in-Parliament)
2. The House of Lords (an upper house, but in fact the second chamber)
3. The House of Commons (a so-called "lower house", but in fact the primary chamber)
