What is the significance of the Third Reading in the Government Bill passing process?
The Third Reading is the stage of a legislative process in which a bill is read with all amendments and given final approval by a legislative body. At this stage, the entire legislature gives consideration to its passage, and the bill may be studied in detail, debated, amended, and read at length before final passage. If the majority vote in favor of the bill, it is recorded as passed.
