How did party lines work in terms of technical infrastructure and user experience?
Party lines worked by sharing a single local loop telephone circuit among multiple subscribers. This meant that all users on the same party line could hear each other's conversations, providing no privacy in communication. The technical infrastructure consisted of electro-mechanical switching equipment, which was later replaced by electronic and digital switching equipment. In terms of user experience, party lines were often used as a source of entertainment and gossip, and also served as a means of quickly alerting entire neighborhoods of emergencies. However, they were prone to traffic congestion, especially during peak usage times, which could lead to poor transmission quality.
