To find the possible integer values of the cube root of 6,859, I can use the fact that the cube of any cube root of 8 is 8. Since 6,859 is not equal to 8, I will look for the nearest perfect cube that is less than or equal to 6,859.

The nearest perfect cube less than or equal to 6,859 is 6,561 (which is the cube of 9), and the next perfect cube greater than 6,859 is 7,401 (which is the cube of 9.5).

Therefore, the possible integer values of the cube root of 6,859 are the integers between the cube roots of 6,561 and 7,401, which are:

9 ≤ cube root of 6,859 ≤ 9.5

Since the cube root of 6,859 is not an integer, the possible integer values of the cube root of 6,859 are 9 and 10.
