What is the physical significance of the ratio of velocities of light in two adjacent media?
The physical significance of the ratio of velocities of light in two adjacent media is that it is equal to the ratio of the sines of the angles of incidence and refraction, as stated by Snell's law. This ratio is also equivalent to the reciprocal of the ratio of the indices of refraction of the two media.
